Corpus of Go template sources, shared by the Go oracle and the TypeScript tests.

Each entry is one template source. The Go oracle (oracle/main.go) parses every
entry with text/template and html/template and records whether it parsed and
what the error said, into expected.json. The TypeScript differential test reads
that same file and checks our parser agrees about which entries are broken.

Format is Go's txtar: a "-- name --" line starts a new entry, everything up to
the next such line is its content.

Names are prefixed by what they are testing:
  ok-      expected to parse
  lex-     expected to fail in the lexer
  parse-   expected to fail in the parser (structure)
  sem-     expected to fail on a semantic check (scope, funcs, duplicates)
  num-     number literal syntax

-- ok-empty --
-- ok-text-only --
hello world
-- ok-text-with-newlines --
line one
line two

line four
